Factual Metal Launcher - Real Steel (Linux, x86_64) @VERSION@
==========================================================

A native Linux port of Yuke's "Real Steel" (Xbox 360 XBLA,
title ID 584111E0), recompiled with the ReXGlue SDK, with a bespoke
Qt launcher. One AppImage contains the launcher and the game program;
it does NOT contain any game data.

YOU NEED: your own legally obtained XBLA package of Real Steel
(the STFS package file for title 584111E0). The import accepts the
package file directly, or a .rar / .zip / .7z archive containing
it. No game data is included and none will be downloaded.

FIRST RUN
  1. Run RealSteel-x86_64-@VERSION@.AppImage.
  2. Click "Import XBLA package or archive..." and pick your
     package file or archive. It is extracted to a data folder
     you choose.
  3. Click PLAY.

GAME SPEED
  Real Steel's game logic advances once per frame, so the game runs
  at its real speed only at 60 fps. Keep Settings > Frame limit at 60
  (the default). Lower frame rates play in slow motion; "unlimited"
  runs the game too fast. VSync is on by default and only removes
  tearing - it never slows the game down.

SETTINGS (all optional, saved automatically, Reset button included)
  Graphics: internal resolution scale (720p/1440p/2160p), AMD FSR or
  bilinear upscaling, FXAA, native 2x MSAA, anisotropic filtering,
  async shader compilation, vsync, fullscreen/windowed, frame limit.
  On a weak or integrated GPU: keep 720p (1x) and pick Bilinear
  upscaling - FSR runs at your full display resolution every frame.
  Audio: mute.
  Storage: choose where saves/profile data and log files are stored.
  Advanced: Vulkan options and profile locale - leave these alone
  unless you are experimenting.

GOOD TO KNOW
  - Online versus is stubbed out: this is an offline build
    (single player and local play work).
  - The DLC fighters were separate downloads on the Xbox 360 and
    are not part of the base package, so those roster slots stay
    locked unless you supply data that includes them.

REQUIREMENTS
  - 64-bit Linux (x86_64) with a Vulkan-capable GPU and driver.
  - A gamepad is strongly recommended (Xbox-style pads work).
  - Compatibility note: this build was produced on Ubuntu 26.04 and
    needs glibc 2.43 or newer.

TROUBLESHOOTING
  - If the game ever fails to start after a crash, remove any stale
    xenia_memory_* files from /dev/shm and run it again.
  - Logs: see the logs folder inside your data folder
    (last-command.txt shows the exact launch arguments).
  - Frame-rate diagnostics: add --rs_perf_log=true to the game's
    command line; the log then shows fps every 2 seconds.

CREDITS & LICENSES
  This project's own code is BSD 3-Clause. Full attribution for
  every library and tool used (ReXGlue SDK, Qt, 7-Zip, FidelityFX,
  FFmpeg, SDL and more) is inside the AppImage under
  usr/share/licenses/realsteel/ and in CREDITS.md in the source
  repository: https://github.com/thefixinhixon/RealSteelRecomp

No game data, artwork, or other assets from the original game are
distributed with this package.
